### Create a new product
POST http://localhost:3002/products
content-type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nike Air Max 90",
  "slug": "nike-air-max-90-premium",
  "description": "Iconic sneaker with premium leather and Air cushioning.",
  "basePrice": 129.99,
  "isActive": true,
  "attributes": {
    "brand": "Nike",
    "color": "White/Red",
    "material": "Leather & Mesh",
    "weight_grams": 380
  },
  "categoryId": "2ea98950-f179-4ac1-8166-9c5b626f3f67",
  "tagIds": [
    "f9a52eff-eb42-4eb6-897c-b9927b85b075"
  ]
}

### Catalog page 1 (default page size = 24)
GET http://localhost:3002/products

### Catalog page 1 with explicit limit
GET http://localhost:3002/products?limit=24

### Limit clamp check (returns at most 48 items)
GET http://localhost:3002/products?limit=999

### Next page (paste a nextCursor from a previous response)
GET http://localhost:3002/products?cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE

### Tampered cursor -> expect HTTP 400
GET http://localhost:3002/products?cursor=not-a-real-cursor

### Featured rail (plain CatalogProductCard[], only isFeatured, default cap 12)
GET http://localhost:3002/products/featured

### Featured rail with explicit limit
GET http://localhost:3002/products/featured?limit=6

### Trending rail (plain CatalogProductCard[], only isTrending)
GET http://localhost:3002/products/trending

### Categories rail (plain CategoryRailItem[] of { id, name, slug })
GET http://localhost:3002/products/categories

